ReadRaw swallows the os.ReadFile error when the helper guard os.IsNotExist(err) holds
and returns it unwrapped otherwise. Expected: the origins of ReadFile's os.Open (an
Unresolved captured variable under *fs.PathError.Unwrap) and of its f.Read (poll and
errno values, mostly under *fs.PathError.Unwrap; io.EOF is turned into nil inside
ReadFile and must not appear), each kept and marked "possibly handled: guarded by call
to os.IsNotExist" (a helper guard cannot be decided). ReadFile discards the results of
f.Stat and of the deferred f.Close, which contribute nothing. No fmt.Errorf link, and
no entry for the default-document path.
